hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1481","It was narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala, narrated by Sufyan, Abu al-Zinad narrated to me, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Ibn Ajlan and others, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I intended to order my boys to perform the prayer, and to order some of the boys to leave behind to meet the men who were staying behind in the prayer.” So they will burn their houses against them, and if one of them knew that he was being called to eat something, to eat porridge, that is, he would have responded.”"
"1482","Abu Bakr said: As for the news of Ibn Ajlan that Ibn Uyaynah sent, it was only narrated by Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was narrated by Bundar. Safwan and Abu Asim narrated to me, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, and he mentioned the hadith."
